{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01478",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.77,
      "end_seconds": 7.96,
      "duration_seconds": 7.19,
      "text": "Doctor, hi, where would you like me to to put my coat?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.27,
      "end_seconds": 15.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "no problem at all, come in what's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 17.17,
      "end_seconds": 24.39,
      "duration_seconds": 7.22,
      "text": "Okay, you know, so morning, doctor. I'll stay and fill in anything that's missed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.85,
      "end_seconds": 29.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.05,
      "end_seconds": 34.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "I've been dealing with skipped beats."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.25,
      "end_seconds": 38.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.38,
      "end_seconds": 42.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Since last weekend, that's when it began."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.87,
      "end_seconds": 49.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.19,
      "end_seconds": 80.66,
      "duration_seconds": 30.47,
      "text": "It's on and off. I notice it more with lying down and caffeine. Maybe a five out of ten on a bad day. I get some relief from deep breaths. Right, I've also had a flutter in my chest, for about three months. Let me think, I had being a bit anxious before. That's settled now, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.36,
      "end_seconds": 86.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Okay, and what about shortness of breath or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.27,
      "end_seconds": 92.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "No, um, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.88,
      "end_seconds": 96.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "a few quick ones: fainting or dizziness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.06,
      "end_seconds": 103.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "I haven't had fainting or dizziness, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.01,
      "end_seconds": 108.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Alright, neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.04,
      "end_seconds": 111.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "erm, no, that's all normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.6,
      "end_seconds": 116.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.02,
      "end_seconds": 120.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "no, that's all fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.87,
      "end_seconds": 126.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.81,
      "end_seconds": 155.54,
      "duration_seconds": 27.73,
      "text": "I mean, I have heart disease, for two years. Yeah, I've had an irregular heartbeat for five years now. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. I have low haemoglobin. Actually, I have an underactive thyroid, for about a year. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.21,
      "end_seconds": 167.79,
      "duration_seconds": 10.58,
      "text": "Sure. Right, so an underactive thyroid is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.26,
      "end_seconds": 175.42,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "No, um, not that that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 176.08,
      "end_seconds": 184.66,
      "duration_seconds": 8.58,
      "text": "actually, I remember she had some kind of reaction to diclofenac before i couldn't swear to it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.73,
      "end_seconds": 188.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "I don't remember that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.61,
      "end_seconds": 196.13,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "Okay, I'll note both of those. What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.33,
      "end_seconds": 202.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.43,
      "text": "Yes, I had part of my thyroid removed, years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.36,
      "end_seconds": 217.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 218.51,
      "end_seconds": 226.13,
      "duration_seconds": 7.62,
      "text": "let me think, she is on clopidogrel, once a day, I give it to her"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.7,
      "end_seconds": 229.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "so, how much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 231.17,
      "end_seconds": 232.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "it's 75 milligrams"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.39,
      "end_seconds": 236.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "roughly how long on that one?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 237.08,
      "end_seconds": 260.02,
      "duration_seconds": 22.94,
      "text": "for nearly five years hmm, um, she is on apixaban, 5 milligrams, twice a day for the heart rhythm, I give it it to her well, um, it's iron tablets, once a day, doctor it's Eltroxin, 100 micrograms, every morning for my thyroid, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.0,
      "end_seconds": 267.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Before this I was on aspirin; that's been stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.88,
      "end_seconds": 270.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.75,
      "end_seconds": 275.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "I have about eight cigarettes in a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.92,
      "end_seconds": 278.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.27,
      "end_seconds": 284.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "I'll have a glass of wine with dinner"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.55,
      "end_seconds": 288.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Okay, are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.01,
      "end_seconds": 296.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.55,
      "end_seconds": 299.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.24,
      "end_seconds": 304.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.07,
      "end_seconds": 307.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "alright, tell me about your eating"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.89,
      "end_seconds": 314.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.91,
      "end_seconds": 320.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.21,
      "end_seconds": 328.7,
      "duration_seconds": 7.49,
      "text": "My uncle has high cholesterol. Let me think, you know, my cousin has psoriasis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.11,
      "end_seconds": 344.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.2,
      "end_seconds": 360.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Right, keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 380.87,
      "end_seconds": 386.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "Okay: temperature is 36.9 degrees, BP is 120 over 68, pulse 69."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 388.37,
      "end_seconds": 393.81,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 394.69,
      "end_seconds": 397.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 415.19,
      "end_seconds": 419.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Your pulse is regular and your heart sounds are normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 422.78,
      "end_seconds": 424.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "You can relax now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 438.65,
      "end_seconds": 446.05,
      "duration_seconds": 7.4,
      "text": "Having listened and examined, my working impression is harmless extra heartbeats. Another possibility is an anxiety-related palpitation."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 447.37,
      "end_seconds": 451.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "I'm, I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 453.74,
      "end_seconds": 481.07,
      "duration_seconds": 27.33,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's harmless extra heartbeats, and we'll know more once the an ECG is back. Let's book an ECG to look into palpitations. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. Cut back on coffee and energy drinks and keep a diary of when it happens. We'll catch up if it carries on after a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 483.12,
      "end_seconds": 483.82,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "right"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 485.37,
      "end_seconds": 487.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 488.8,
      "end_seconds": 495.22,
      "duration_seconds": 6.42,
      "text": "Um, um, okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 500.77,
      "end_seconds": 502.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ]
}